WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.610
A baby born in Norway in 2023
could expect to live 83.3 years.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.610
A baby born in Somalia: 58.8 years.

3
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.250
A gap of about 25 years, set
by where a child is born.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.330
The UN ranks countries
on human development.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.930
Iceland is top.

6
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.450
South Sudan is bottom of 193.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.730
So why does where you are
born make such a difference?

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:27.930
Is it the heat?

9
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:28.530
Is it the diet?

10
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.610
In this mission, you'll
measure the development gap,

11
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.650
and weigh what drives it.

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.330
Then you'll use those causes to predict
what happens to a country under pressure.

13
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: explain why life expectancy
differs so much between Norway and Somalia.
